GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 81: the Government's further standards for controllers and the Minister of Finance's rules on degrees and certificates` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 81 delegates further standards for controllers to the Government and the detail of the degree and certificate rules to the Minister of Finance; neither is among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 82: holding more than one post`

-- Dieu 82(4). The actuary, the head of risk management and the head of compliance control may hold no other
-- management post in the same organisation and may not work at another insurer. V2 (Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(6)(a))
-- adds one exception: the actuary may also head the pricing department. Dieu 82(6) likewise for the chief accountant
-- and the head of internal audit: V2 (Dieu 1(6)(b)) lets the chief accountant also head finance and accounting.
@@q 1625 1631
@@qa 142 151
@ref Dieu 82 (src:1625-1631; src:law139-2025-qh15:142-151)
GIVEN p IS A `A person's posts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 82(4): the actuary, head of risk management or head of compliance control holds an allowed combination of posts` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `main post`
    WHEN `actuary` THEN
            (   null (p's `other posts held in the same organisation`)
             OR (    `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
                 AND p's `other posts held in the same organisation` EQUALS LIST `head of the pricing department`))
        AND (NOT p's `works at another insurer, reinsurer or foreign branch in Vietnam at the same time`)
    WHEN `head of risk management` THEN null (p's `other posts held in the same organisation`) AND (NOT p's `works at another insurer, reinsurer or foreign branch in Vietnam at the same time`)
    WHEN `head of compliance control` THEN null (p's `other posts held in the same organisation`) AND (NOT p's `works at another insurer, reinsurer or foreign branch in Vietnam at the same time`)
    OTHERWISE REFUSE "Dieu 82(4) governs the actuary, the head of risk management and the head of compliance control"

@@q 1636 1640
@@qa 156 163
@ref Dieu 82 (src:1636-1640; src:law139-2025-qh15:156-163)
GIVEN p IS A `A person's posts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 82(6): the chief accountant or head of internal audit holds an allowed combination of posts` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `main post`
    WHEN `chief accountant` THEN
            (   null (p's `other posts held in the same organisation`)
             OR (    `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
                 AND p's `other posts held in the same organisation` EQUALS LIST `head of finance and accounting`))
        AND (NOT p's `works at another insurer, reinsurer or foreign branch in Vietnam at the same time`)
    WHEN `head of internal audit` THEN null (p's `other posts held in the same organisation`) AND (NOT p's `works at another insurer, reinsurer or foreign branch in Vietnam at the same time`)
    OTHERWISE REFUSE "Dieu 82(6) governs the chief accountant and the head of internal audit"

@@q 1605 1624
@ref Dieu 82 (src:1605-1624)
`Dieu 82(1)-(3), (5) — a board member may not sit on the board of another insurer in the same field; a chief executive may not work for another insurer in the same field; a chief executive, branch director or head of a representative office may also be at most one branch director, or head of one representative office, or head of one business department of the same insurer; the head of the supervisory board and controllers hold no management post at the same organisation (principles of holding office; each is a fact about posts held at the date of appointment; the two amended paragraphs (4) and (6) are encoded above)` MEANS
    "Principles of holding office."

§§ `Dieu 83: suspending officers`

@@q 1644 1664
@ref Dieu 83 (src:1644-1664)
`Dieu 83(1) — the Ministry of Finance may suspend the chair, the chief executive or the actuary who breaches Dieu 82 or no longer meets Dieu 81 (a power exercised on those facts)` MEANS
    "A power of the Ministry of Finance."

GIVEN v IS A `A vacancy`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 83(2): the last day to file a valid dossier for a replacement after a suspension` v MEANS
    v's `date the Ministry of Finance suspended the officer` PLUS 75

@@q 1661 1664
